# P.Sonkar House of Ventures — Project Configuration

## Project Overview
P.Sonkar House of Ventures is a 3D immersive marketing website + admin CMS for a founder-led venture studio in Bangalore, India. The site features WebGL 3D scenes on every page, scroll-driven animations, and a dark premium aesthetic.

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router) with TypeScript
- **3D Engine**: Three.js via React Three Fiber (@react-three/fiber)
- **3D Helpers**: @react-three/drei (Float, Text3D, Environment, Stars, MeshDistortMaterial, Sparkles)
- **Post-processing**: @react-three/postprocessing (Bloom, Vignette, ChromaticAberration)
- **Scroll Animations**: GSAP + ScrollTrigger (scroll-driven 3D camera/object animations)
- **2D Animations**: Framer Motion (page transitions, text reveals, UI micro-interactions)
- **Smooth Scroll**: Lenis
- **Styling**: Vanilla CSS with CSS Modules (NO Tailwind)
- **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod validation
- **Icons**: Lucide React
- **Database**: PostgreSQL via Supabase
- **ORM**: Prisma
- **Auth**: NextAuth.js v5 (single admin login)
- **File Storage**: Supabase Storage
- **Email**: Resend (transactional)
- **Hosting**: Vercel

## Project Structure
- `src/app/` — Next.js App Router pages and API routes
- `src/components/three/` — All 3D scene components (React Three Fiber)
- `src/components/ui/` — Reusable 2D UI primitives
- `src/components/layout/` — Header, Footer, Navigation, SmoothScroll
- `src/components/sections/` — Page section compositions (home/, about/, etc.)
- `src/components/forms/` — All 4 form components
- `src/components/admin/` — Admin portal components
- `src/hooks/` — Custom hooks (useGPUDetect, useScrollProgress, useReducedMotion)
- `src/lib/` — Utilities (prisma client, auth config, gpu-tier detection)
- `src/shaders/` — Custom GLSL shaders (glass, particles, noise)
- `src/styles/` — CSS design system (globals.css, variables.css, component modules)
- `prisma/` — Database schema and migrations
- `public/models/` — 3D model files (.glb/.gltf)
- `public/textures/` — HDRI environment maps, noise textures

## Architecture Decisions

### 3D Performance Strategy
- All text content is server-side rendered (SSR) for SEO crawlability
- 3D scenes are client-only ("use client") overlay components
- GPU capability detection via `renderer.capabilities` — serve simplified scenes on low-end devices
- WebGL fallback: if unavailable, degrade to 2D Framer Motion animations
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` media query
- Use `instancedMesh` for particle systems, throttle `useFrame` callbacks
- Lazy-load 3D scenes with loading shimmer/skeleton
- Tree-shake Three.js — only import used geometries/materials
- Code-split 3D scenes per page

### Styling Rules
- Use CSS Modules for component-scoped styles
- Global design tokens in `src/styles/variables.css` (colors, spacing, typography, breakpoints)
- Dark theme: deep navy/charcoal backgrounds with vibrant accent glows
- Typography: Outfit (headings) + Inter (body) from Google Fonts
- NO Tailwind CSS — all vanilla CSS

### Component Patterns
- 3D components go in `src/components/three/` and are always `"use client"`
- Every 3D scene component is wrapped in `SceneWrapper` which handles Canvas, GPU detection, fallback
- Page sections are compositions in `src/components/sections/{page}/`
- Forms use React Hook Form with Zod schemas defined inline or in `src/lib/schemas.ts`

### Database
- PostgreSQL hosted on Supabase
- Prisma ORM for type-safe queries and migrations
- Models: Venture, Application, SiteSetting, AdminLog, AdminUser
- All admin actions logged with timestamp in AdminLog table

### Authentication
- NextAuth.js v5 with Credentials provider (single admin login)
- Admin routes protected via middleware and session checks
- No public registration — admin seeded directly in database

### SEO
- Every page has SSR-rendered content (3D is decorative overlay only)
- JSON-LD schema markup: Organization, Person, WebSite
- Dynamic OG images via `next/og`
- Auto-generated sitemap.xml via Next.js metadata API
- Canonical URLs on every page
- Venture cards have anchor URLs for deep linking

## Key Files
- `src/app/layout.tsx` — Root layout with fonts, metadata, SmoothScroll provider
- `src/components/three/SceneWrapper.tsx` — Canvas + GPU detection + fallback wrapper
- `src/components/three/HeroScene.tsx` — Home page 3D hero scene
- `src/styles/variables.css` — Design tokens (colors, spacing, typography)
- `src/styles/globals.css` — Global styles, reset, base typography
- `prisma/schema.prisma` — Database schema
- `src/lib/auth.ts` — NextAuth configuration
- `src/lib/prisma.ts` — Prisma client singleton

## Conventions
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Use `@/` import alias for `src/`
- Component files: PascalCase (e.g., `HeroScene.tsx`)
- CSS Module files: camelCase matching component (e.g., `heroScene.module.css`)
- API routes: lowercase kebab-case
- Commit messages: conventional commits format
- All 3D scene components must handle loading states and WebGL fallbacks
- All forms must have both client-side (Zod) and server-side validation
- Admin actions must be logged to AdminLog table
